cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Hurray in your research, please cite the survey paper under
  "preferred-citation" below rather than this repository.
title: Hurray
abstract: >-
  A zero-copy, streamable, language-agnostic tensor interchange format for AI/ML
  inference pipelines and scientific arrays. Hurray defines a language-independent
  descriptor for a tensor's element type, shape, memory layout, quantization, device
  placement, buffers, and composition. The same descriptor encoding is shared by a
  self-delimiting streaming format for runtime interchange and a file format with a
  footer index for random access and mmap-based zero-copy loading.
type: software
