# No version or date-released yet: 0.1.0 is unreleased and the repository carries no
# tags. Add both here when the first release is cut, so the citation names a fixed state.
preferred-citation:
  type: report
  title: >-
    Tensor Data Interchange for AI/ML Systems: A Survey and the Hurray Proposal
  abstract: >-
    A survey of tensor interchange solutions — DLPack, Apache Arrow, SafeTensors, GGUF,
    Zarr, NetCDF, ONNX, NIXL, UCX, and NCCL — comparing the tensor information each one
    preserves. The comparison shows a practical gap for tensors whose physical
    representation matters to computation: layout, quantization, device memory, paging,
    and sharding increasingly appear at the boundaries between runtimes, yet no widely
    used interchange format combines them in one tensor description reusable across
    memory, files, and network transfers. The paper then presents Hurray, an
    open-source tensor interchange project designed for this use case.
  authors:
    - family-names: Gillet
      given-names: Pascal
      email: pascalgillet@ymail.com
      # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
  year: 2026
  month: 9
  doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23023990
  url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23023990"
  license: CC-BY-4.0
  keywords:
    - tensor interchange
    - zero-copy
    - DLPack
    - Apache Arrow
    - GGUF
    - SafeTensors
    - quantization
    - KV cache
    - disaggregated inference
